 65      COMMENTS                                                25NDS    202505
 65    H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65   C  TITL$Nuclear Structure and Decay data for A=65 isobars                 
 65   c  AUTH$Jun Chen                                                          
 65   c  INST$Facility for Rare Isotope Beams,                                  
 65  #c       Michigan State University,                                        
 65  #c       East Lansing, Michigan 48824, USA.                                
 65   c  ABST$Experimental nuclear structure and decay data are evaluated for   
 65  2c  13 known nuclides of mass number A=65 (V, Cr, Mn, Fe, Co, Ni, Cu, Zn,  
 65  3c  Ga Ge, As, Se, Br). Detailed evaluated level properties and related    
 65  4c  information are presented and recommended spectroscopic parameters are 
 65  5c  provided, combining all the data from various reactions and decays. At 
 65  6c  the proton-rich end, {+65}Br has been studied theoretically but still  
 65  7c  remains unobserved experimentally, while at the neutron-rich end,      
 65  8c  {+65}V has been observed, but its ground-state T{-1/2} and J|p wait to 
 65  9c  be measured and determined. No excited state has been observed for     
 65  ac  {+65}V, {+65}Cr, and {+65}Se. The ground-state spins and/or parities   
 65  bc  of {+65}Fe, {+65}Co, {+65}Ge, {+65}As, and {+65}Se still have not been 
 65  cc  definitely determined. Information for excited states in {+65}Mn and   
 65  dc  {+65}As is very limited. {+65}Cu is the most extensively studied via   
 65  ec  26 different reactions and decays, followed by {+65}Zn and {+65}Ga.    
 65  fc  For {+65}Co and {+65}Ni, their radioactive decay schemes are           
 65  gc  incomplete.  This work supersedes earlier full evaluations of A=65     
 65  hc  published by 2010Br10, 1993Bh04, 1986Wa02, and 1975Au08.               
 65   c  CUT$Literature available up to February 25, 2025 has been consulted,   
 65  2c  with the help of the primary bibliographic source, the NSR database    
 65  3c  (2011Pr03) available at Brookhaven National Laboratory web page:       
 65  #c  www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/                                                  
 65   c  COMM$The statistical analysis of |g-ray data and deduced level schemes 
 65  2c  is carried out through a suite of computer codes such as GLSC and      
 65  3c  Java-RULER available at IAEA-Nuclear Data Sheets web page. The direct  
 65  4c  feedings to excited states in |b{+-} and |e decays have generally been 
 65  5c  computed from I(|g+ce) intensity balances at each level; the           
 65  6c  associated log {Ift} values are calculated using the BetaShape code    
 65  7c  (2023Mo21).  Theoretical total conversion coefficients are calculated  
 65  8c  using the BrIcc code (2008Ki07) for the "Frozen-orbitals" option. In   
 65  9c  cases where weighted averaging procedures have been used, the assigned 
 65  ac  uncertainty in the result is generally not lower than the lowest       
 65  bc  uncertainty amongst the data points used in the procedure.             
 65   c  ACKN$Earlier evaluations (2010Br10, 1993Bh04, 1986Wa02, 1975Au08), and 
 65  2c  compilations in the XUNDL database provided valuable resources for the 
 65  3c  present work. The evaluator is grateful to the reviewers for detailed  
 65  4c  review at different stages of this work, and to the personnel at the   
 65  5c  National Nuclear Data Center (NNDC) at Brookhaven National Laboratory  
 65  6c  for facilitating this work.                                            
 65   c  CIT$NDS 202, 59 (2025)                                                 
 65   c  PERM$Contacts: chenj@frib.msu.edu FUND$ Work supported by the Office   
 65  2c  of Nuclear Physics, Office of Science, U.S. Department of Energy,      
 65  3c  through |DE-SC0016948 grant at the Michigan State University           

