 65V 2cQ (syst,2021Wa16)                                                        
 65V  c  2009Ta05,2009Ta24: {+65}V was identified by fragmentation of {+76}Ge   
 65V 2c  beam at 132 MeV/nucleon at NSCL facility using A1900 fragment          
 65V 3c  separator combined with S800 analysis beam line to form a two-stage    
 65V 4c  separator system. The transmitted fragments were analyzed              
 65V 5c  event-by-event in momentum and particle identification. The nuclei of  
 65V 6c  interest were stopped in eight Si diodes which provided measurement of 
 65V 7c  energy loss, nuclear charge and total kinetic energy. The              
 65V 8c  time-of-flight of each particle that reached the detector stack was    
 65V 9c  measured in four different ways using plastic scintillators, Si        
 65V ac  detectors, and parallel-plate avalanche counters. The simultaneous     
 65V bc  measurement of |DE signals, the magnetic rigidity, total kinetic       
 65V cc  energy and the time-of-flight (tof) provided unambiguous               
 65V dc  identification of the atomic number, charge state and mass number.     
