 65CR c  Mass measurements: 2022Si20 (M.E.=-28208 {I45}), 2020Me06 (M.E.=-27280 
 65CR2c  {I780})                                                                
 65CR c  2022Si20: {+65}Cr was produced via U(p,X) with a 480 MeV proton beam   
 65CR2c  impinged on a UC{-x} target at the ISAC facility of TRIUMF. Fragments  
 65CR3c  were separated by the ISAC dipole magnetic separator and sent to       
 65CR4c  a Multiple-Reflection Time-of-Flight Mass Spectrometer (|d-tof-ms) of  
 65CR5c  the TITAN facility. Measured time-of-flight, storage time. Deduced     
 65CR6c  mass excess, T{-1/2}                                                   
 65CR c  2020Me06: {+65}Cr was produced by fragmentation of a 140 MeV/nucleon   
 65CR2c  {+82}Se beam on a Be target at NSCL. Fragments were separated by the   
 65CR3c  A1900 fragment separator, analyzed with the S800 spectrograph, and     
 65CR4c  stopped in the focal plane of S800, with identification using the      
 65CR5c  tof-|DE method. Deduced mass excess from the magnetic-rigidity         
 65CR6c  corrected time-of-flight (tof-B|r) mass spectrometry.                  
 65CR c  2011Da08: {+65}Cr was produced in the fragmentation of 57.8 MeV/nucleon
 65CR2c  {+86}Kr beam impinged on 50 mg/cm{+2} thick tantalum target at GANIL.  
 65CR3c  Fragments were identified and selected using the LISE-2000 spectrometer
 65CR4c  with a three-element Si-detector telescope, and implanted into a       
 65CR5c  double-sided silicon-strip detector (DSSSD) backed by a Si(Li) detector
 65CR6c  and surrounded by four clover type EXOGAM Ge detectors. Measured       
 65CR7c  implant-|b time correlation. Deduced {+65}Cr decay half-life. See      
 65CR8c  also 2002MaZN thesis                                                   
 65CR c  2005Ga01,2003So21: {+65}Cr was produced by fragmentation of a 61.8     
 65CR2c  MeV/nucleon {+76}Ge beam on a {+58}Ni target at GANIL. Fragments were  
 65CR3c  identified and seperated by the LISE3 spectrometer with 3 consecutive  
 65CR4c  silicon detectors, and implanted into the last Si detector surrounded  
 65CR5c  by 4 Ge detectors for |g detection. Measured E|b, |b|g-coin,           
 65CR6c  implant-|b(t). Deduced {+65}Cr decay T{-1/2}.                          
 65CR c  1997Be70: {+65}Cr was produced by fission of uranium projectiles at    
 65CR2c  relativistic energies on a beryllium target at GSI. Identification of  
 65CR3c  fission fragments was done with a fragment separator (FRS) using       
 65CR4c  energy-loss measurements for element identification, and time-of-flight
 65CR5c  and magnetic rigidity for mass determination. Measured production      
 65CR6c  yields. See also 1995CzZZ for their first measurement and preliminary  
 65CR7c  results.                                                               
 65CR c  1995CzZZ: Pb,Be({+238}U,F) E=750 MeV/nucleon at GSI. A preliminary     
 65CR2c  result reveals more than 50 new neutron-rich isotopes ranging from     
 65CR3c  {+62}V to {+120}Ru identified by time-of-flight using the fragment     
 65CR4c  separator FRS. No detailed results are presented. This preliminary     
 65CR5c  report is superseded by 1997Be70.                                      
 65CR c  Theoretical calculation:                                               
 65CR c  2011Gu03: calculated rms radius of p-wave valence neutron distribution.
