 65MN c  2018Li46: E|?260 MeV/nucleon {+68}Fe beam was produced by fragmentation
 65MN2c  of a 345 MeV/nucleon primary {+238}U beam on a {+9}Be target at the    
 65MN3c  RIKEN-RIBF facility. The secondary target was 102(1)-mm-thick liquid   
 65MN4c  hydrogen (LH{-2}). Reaction residues were identified and selected      
 65MN5c  with the BigRIPS before the target and the ZeroDegree spectrometer     
 65MN6c  after target by the B|r-|DE-tof method. Charged particles were         
 65MN7c  detected with the Time-Projection Chamber (TPC) of the MINOS device;   
 65MN8c  |g rays were detected by the DALI2 spectrometer. Measured E|g, I|g,    
 65MN9c  |g|g-coin. Deduced levels, J, |p. Comparisons with large-scale         
 65MNac  shell-model calculations.                                              
