 65FE c  2007Lu13: E=400 MeV {+64}Ni beam was produced from the LNL Tandem-ALPI 
 65FE2c  accelerator. Target was {+238}U. Projectile-like nuclei were identified
 65FE3c  with the PRISMA large acceptance magnetic spectrometer. |g rays were   
 65FE4c  detected with the CLARA array comprised of 25 Clover Ge detectors with 
 65FE5c  Compton-suppression. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin. Deduced levels, J,  
 65FE6c  |p, band structure. Comparisons with shell-model calculations          
 65FE cG E,RI$From 2007Lu13                                                     
 65FE cL E$From E|g data                                                        
