 65FE    66MN B-N DECAY                2017OL08,2018ST18         25NDS    202505
 65FE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65FE dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 17-Jul-2024)          
 65FE c  Adapted from the XUNDL dataset for 2017Ol08 compiled by B. Singh       
 65FE2c  (McMaster) on December 14, 2017 and the XUNDL dataset for 2018St18     
 65FE3c  compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL), on April 16, 2020               
 65FE c  2017Ol08: {+66}Mn source was produced in bombardment of UC{-x} target  
 65FE2c  by 1.4-GeV pulsed protons at the ISOLDE-CERN facility. Reaction        
 65FE3c  products diffused out of the target were ionized by selective          
 65FE4c  resonant ionization using RILIS, mass separated by General Purpose     
 65FE5c  Separator (GPS), and implanted into a thin Al foil. |b particles were  
 65FE6c  detected with a fast-timing plastic scintillator and |g rays were      
 65FE7c  detected with two LaBr{-3}(Ce) and two HPGe detectors. Measured E|g,   
 65FE8c  I|g,|g|g-coin, |b|g(t). Deduced levels, J, |p, parent T{-1/2},         
 65FE9c  |b-delayed neutron emission probability. Comparisons with available    
 65FEac  data and large-scale shell-model calculations with the                 
 65FEbc  Lenzi-Nowacki-Poves-Sieja (LNPS) interaction.                          
 65FE c  2018St18: {+66}Mn activity was produced in U(p,F) reaction with        
 65FE2c  E(p)=1.4 GeV reaction using UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN facility. Mn  
 65FE3c  atoms were ionized using the ISOLDE Resonance Ionization Laser Ion     
 65FE4c  Source (RILIS) followed by mass separation. |b particles were detected 
 65FE5c  with three plastic |DE detectors and |g rays were detected with two    
 65FE6c  HPGe MiniBall cluster detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |b|g(t).
 65FE7c  Deduced levels, J, |p, parent T{-1/2}, isomer T{-1/2}, |b-delayed      
 65FE8c  neutron emission probability. Comparisons with available data and      
 65FE9c  shell-model calculations.                                              
 65FE c  2013Li04: {+66}Mn source was produced at NSCL. Report data for {+66}Mn 
 65FE2c  |b{+-} decay and |b-delayed neutron emission probability               
 65FE cDNIP$Deduced by the evaluator from |g-ray intensity balance at each      
 65FE2cDN level for excited level, with |S%I(|b{+-}n to excited                 
 65FE3cDN level)=100-%I(|b{+-}n to g.s.)=59 {I8}. Values from 2017Ol08 and      
 65FE4cDN 2018St18 are deduced in the same way and are given under comments.    
 65FE cG RI$Relative to I|g=100 of 573.5|g in {+66}Fe from {+66}Mn decay        
 65FE cL E$From E|g data                                                        
 65FE cL J,T$From Adopted Levels                                                
 66MN  P 0.0          (1+)             63.9 MS   11              6396     12    
 66MN cP J$Proposed by 2011Li50 based on systematics of neighboring nuclei      
