 65CO c  Adapted from the XUNDL dataset for 2009Pa16, compiled by B. Karamy and 
 65CO2c  B. Singh (McMaster) on May 12, 2009 including data received from       
 65CO3c  D. Pauwels in an email reply to B. Singh on May 12, 2009               
 65CO c  2009Pa16: E=430 MeV {+64}Ni beam was produced from the ATLAS           
 65CO2c  accelerator at ANL. Target was 55 mg/cm{+2} isotopically-enriched      
 65CO3c  {+238}U. |g rays were detected with the Gammasphere array consisting   
 65CO4c  of 100 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,
 65CO5c  |g|g|g-coin. Deduced levels, J, |p.                                    
 65CO c  2013Mo36: E=460 MeV {+64}Ni beam was produced from the Laboratori      
 65CO2c  Nazionali di Legnaro (LNL) Tandem-ALPI accelerator complex. Target was 
 65CO3c  1.35 mg/cm{+2} {+238}U on 1.2 mg/cm{+2} thick Ta. Projectile-like      
 65CO4c  products were identified with the magnetic spectrometer PRISMA. |g rays
 65CO5c  were detected by the AGATA demonstrator consisting of four triple      
 65CO6c  clusters of Ge detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, particle-|g-coin,         
 65CO7c  recoil-distance Doppler-shift intensity ratio with a plunger. Deduced  
 65CO8c  levels, J, |p, T{-1/2}, configurations. Comparison with large-scale    
 65CO9c  shell-model calculations.                                              
