 65CO cL J(A)$Assignments for 1480 and 1643 levels are inverse in 2009Pa16 in   
 65CO2cL their decay scheme of {+65}Fe |b{+-} decay (1.12 s). 2012Re11 argue    
 65CO3cL that those assignments by 2009Pa16 are mainly based on systematics of  
 65CO4cL neighboring odd-A Co isotopes, but from data in this work, the         
 65CO5cL intensity ratio of the 1480|g and 1643|g is completely different from  
 65CO6cL those for correpsonding transitions in {+61}Co and {+63}Co, which,     
 65CO7cL together with measured R{-asym} of 1480|g suggesting |DJ=2, indicates a
 65CO8cL spin-parity inversion for the two levels as members of the             
 65CO9cL |pf{-7/2}{+-1}|~2{++}({+66}Ni) multiplet, compared to spin-parities of 
 65COacL correspdoning levels in {+61}Co and {+63}Co. 2012Re11 also show that   
 65CObcL their assignments are consistent with the predictions from the         
 65COccL large-scale shell-model calculations using the LNPS interaction        
 65COdcL proposed in 2010Le20                                                   
