 65NI    64NI(D,PG)                    2017CR04,1978MU05,2006GE1625NDS    202505
 65NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65NI c  Adapted from a XUNDL dataset for 2017Cr04, compiled by B. Singh        
 65NI2c  (McMaster University) on August 20, 2017                               
 65NI c  2017Cr04: E=12.5 MeV deuteron beam was produced from the Oslo Cyclotron
 65NI2c  Laboratory (OCL). Target was self-supporting 99% enriched {+64}Ni of 1 
 65NI3c  mg/cm{+2} thickness. Charged particles were detected with the Silicon  
 65NI4c  Ring (SiRi) particle-detector array (FWHM|?120 keV) at 692 keV; |g rays
 65NI5c  were detected with the CACTUS array of 26 collimated NaI(Tl) detectors 
 65NI6c  (FWHM|?70 keV at 1017 keV). Timing resolution (FWHM) for coincidence   
 65NI7c  measurement was |?15 ns. Measured particle spectra, E|g,               
 65NI8c  (particle)|g-coin. Deduced levels, nuclear level-density (NLD) and     
 65NI9c  gamma-strength function (|gSF). The experiment is mainly about         
 65NIac  determination of nuclear level density (NLD) and |g-strength function  
 65NIbc  (|gSF) of {+65}Ni by the Oslo method.                                  
 65NI c  1978Mu05: E=8 MeV pulsed deuteron beam was produced from the FN tandem 
 65NI2c  accelerator at ANL. Target was 2 mg/cm{+2} 98% enriched {+64}Ni.       
 65NI3c  |g rays were detected with a Si(Li) detector. Measured E|g, |g(t).     
 65NI4c  Deduced isomer T{-1/2}.                                                
 65NI c  2006Ge16,2005Ge09: E=6 MeV pulsed deuteron beam was produced from      
 65NI2c  Orsay tandem accelerator. Target was >95% enriched {+64}Ni. |g rays    
 65NI3c  were detected with a pair of Ge and a pair BaF{-2} detectors. Measured 
 65NI4c  E|g, I|g, Time-Dependent Perturbed Angular Distribution (TDPAD).       
 65NI5c  Deduced T{-1/2} and g-factor for the J|p=9/2+ state at 1017 MeV        
 65NI c  1978Ho06: E=12 MeV deuteron beam was produced from the tandem Van de   
 65NI2c  Graaff accelerator at ANL. |g rays were detected with a small Ge(Li)   
 65NI3c  detector. Measured |g(t). Deduced isomer T{-1/2}                       
 65NI cG E$From 2017Cr04, unless otherwise noted                                
