 65NI c  1970Ro22: E=44 MeV |a beam was produced from the Saclay cyclotron.     
 65NI2c  Reaction products were detected with a solid-state analyzer            
 65NI3c  (FWHM=100-150 keV). Measured |s(E{-{+3}He},|q), |q|?10|'-70|'. Deduced 
 65NI4c  levels, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis.  
 65NI5c  Comparisons with available data and theoretical calculations.          
 65NI c  2013Sc06,2013ScZZ: E=38 MeV |a beam was produced from Yale tandem      
 65NI2c  accelerator of WNSL facility. Target was 160 |mg/cm{+2} {+62}Ni (91.0% 
 65NI3c  enriched). Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with a split-pole  
 65NI4c  Enge spectrograph (FWHM|?50 keV). Measured |s(E{-{+3}He},|q). Deduced  
 65NI5c  levels, J, |p, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis. Comparison    
 65NI6c  with shell-model calculations. Cross section are from 2013ScZZ         
 65NI c  Others:                                                                
 65NI c  1961Sa09: E=43 MeV from the Saclay cyclotron. Measured energy          
 65NI2c  spectrum.                                                              
 65NI c  1995Fo19: E=120 MeV from the AVF cyclotron at KVI Groningen. Measured  
 65NI2c  neutron decay of high-lying unbound states                             
