 65NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65NI dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 28-Aug-2024)          
 65NI c  Adapted from a XUNDL dataset for 2020Po12 compiled by B. Singh         
 65NI2c  (McMaster) on December 24, 2020                                        
 65NI c  (n,|g) E=thermal                                                       
 65NI c  2020Po12: thermal neutron beam was obtained from the ILL-Grenoble      
 65NI2c  reactor facility. Target was 86.7 mg, 99.6% enriched {+64}Ni placed    
 65NI3c  at a distance of 9 c.m. from the FIssion Product Prompt gamma-ray      
 65NI4c  Spectrometer (FIPPS) array of eight HPGe detectors. Measured E|g,      
 65NI5c  I|g, |g|g-coin with a time window of 300 ns, |g|g(|q). Deduced levels, 
 65NI6c  J, |p, mixing ratios. Comparison of low-lying structure with           
 65NI7c  Monte Carlo Shell Model (MCSM) calculations.                           
 65NI c  1977Is01: thermal neutrons were produced from the McMaster Nuclear     
 65NI2c  Reactor. Target was 98.02% enriched {+64}Ni. |g rays were detected     
 65NI3c  with an Ge(Li)-NaI(Tl) pair spectrometer. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced   
 65NI4c  levels, absolute photon intensities. Report 22 transitions.            
 65NI c  1972Co31: thermal neutrons were produced from the Brookhaven High      
 65NI2c  Flux Beam Reactor (HFBR). Target was 97.92% enriched {+64}Ni. |g rays  
 65NI3c  were detected with Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,     
 65NI4c  |g(t). Deduced levels, limit of isomer lifetime, absolute photon       
 65NI5c  intensities. 1972Co31 also report data for {+65}Ni |b{+-} decay.       
 65NI c  1971Ar39: thermal neutrons were produced from the 1-MW heavy-water     
 65NI2c  reactor R1 in Stockholm. Target was 97.92% enriched {+64}Ni. |g rays   
 65NI3c  were detected with a Ge(Li) pair spectrometer. Measured E|g, I|g.      
 65NI4c  Deduced levels, absolute photon intensities. Report 12 transitions.    
 65NI5c  The authors state that the uncertainty in relative intensity is 10%    
 65NI6c  strong transitions and increases successively to about 100% for weak   
 65NI7c  ones.                                                                  
 65NI c  Others: 2008He01 (%I|g for 6035|g), 1997Ve03 (cross sections), 1971GiZL
 65NI2c  (a few primary |g rays), 1972GrZA (capture on Ni isotopes)             
 65NI c  (pol n,|g) E=thermal                                                   
 65NI c  1978Ve06: polarized neutron beam was produced from the high-flux       
 65NI2c  reactor (HFR) of the Rector Centrum Nederland at Petten, Netherlands.  
 65NI3c  Target was enriched {+64}Ni. |g rays were detected with a polarization 
 65NI4c  spectrometer consisting of two Ge(Li) detectors and a Permendur        
 65NI5c  polarimeter. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(circ pol). Deduced levels, J, |p.   
 65NI cG E,RI$From 2020Po12 with intensity from |g|g-coin data, unless otherwise
 65NI2cG noted. Quoted values of intensities are relative to I|g(310|g)=100.    
 65NI3cG Original values in 1977Is01, 1972Co31, 1971Ar39 are absolute           
 65NI4cG intensities per 100 neutron captures and have been renormalized by the 
 65NI5cG evaluator to I|g(310|g)=100, as quoted in comments. Note that since    
 65NI6cG I|g(310|g) is not reported in 1977Is01 and I|g(6035) is not available  
 65NI7cG in 2020Po12, the evaluator has used I|g(5788|g) available in both      
 65NI8cG 1977Is01 and 2020Po12 for renormalization.                             
 65NI cG M,MR$As given by 2020Po12, based on their |g|g(|q) data, |g(circ, pol),
 65NI2cG and proposed level scheme, with weak E2 or M2 admixture given in       
 65NI3cG parentheses, even though |d(Q/D) does not overlap zero. When the Mult  
 65NI4cG assignments are consided in Adopted Gammas, the firm assignments of    
 65NI5cG magnetic or electric characters will be placed in parenthsises if there
 65NI6cG are no other strong supporting arguments, since |g|g(|q) data don't    
 65NI7cG give assignments of magnetic or electric characters.                   
