 65NI    64NI(D,P),(POL D,P)           1970AN25,2013SC06         25NDS    202505
 65NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65NI c  Target J|p({+64}Ni g.s.)=0+                                            
 65NI c  (d,p) measurements:                                                    
 65NI c  1970An25: E=7.5 MeV deuteron beam was produced from the MIT-ONR Van de 
 65NI2c  Graaff accelerator. Target was 60 |mg/cm{+2} 95.90% enriched {+62}Ni.  
 65NI3c  Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with the MIT multi-gap        
 65NI4c  spectrograph (FWHM|?13 keV). Measured |s(E{-p},|q),                    
 65NI5c  |q{-lab}|?20|'-170|'. Deduced levels, L-transfers, spectroscopic       
 65NI6c  factors from DWBA analysis. Comparisons with shell-model calculations  
 65NI7c  and available data. See also a preliminary report in 1961En07 and an   
 65NI8c  updated report in 1962Ro19 (same authors for both) from the same lab.  
 65NI9c  Note that there are some discrepancies between L assignments for some  
 65NIac  levels in 1970An25 and 1962Ro19 and that some levels reported in       
 65NIbc  1962Ro19 are not reported in 1970An25. Considering those measurements  
 65NIcc  from the same lab, high resolution in 1970An25, and lack of details in 
 65NIdc  1962Ro19 (the whole report is only a table), the evaluator has used    
 65NIec  data only from 1970An25 which is considered to supersede 1961En07 and  
 65NIfc  1962Ro19.                                                              
 65NI c  1963Fu04: E=15 MeV deuteron beam was produced from University of       
 65NI2c  Pittsburgh cyclotron. Target was about 2 mg/cm{+2} thick foil of       
 65NI3c  {+62}Ni. Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with a magnetic      
 65NI4c  spectrograph (FWHM=45 keV). Measured |s(E{-p},|q), |q{-lab}=9|'-50|'.  
 65NI5c  Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA    
 65NI6c  analysis. Uncertainty in cross-section is about 20%                    
 65NI c  1967Te02: E=7.0-7.5 MeV deuteron beams were produced from the AWRE     
 65NI2c  accelerator at Aldermaston. Target was 100 |mg/cm{+2} 98.56% enriched  
 65NI3c  {+64}Ni. Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with the AWRE        
 65NI4c  magnetic spectrograph (FHWM=15 KeV). Measured |s(E{-p}). Deduced       
 65NI5c  levels. Comparisons with available data.                               
 65NI c  1970Tu02: E=11.5 MeV deuteron beam was produced from the Saclay Van de 
 65NI2c  Graaff accelerator. Targets were 100-200 |mg/cm{+2} 99.02% enriched    
 65NI3c  {+62}Ni on carbon backings. Reaction products were momentum-analyzed   
 65NI4c  with a magnetic spectrograph (FWHM|?25-30 keV). Measured |s(E{-p},|q), 
 65NI5c  |q{-cm}=5|'-60|'. Deduced levels, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors   
 65NI6c  from DWBA analysis. Accuracy of cross-sections is estimated to be      
 65NI7c  between 10%-20%. Note that the 1970Tu02 have adopted level energies    
 65NI8c  from 1967Te02                                                          
 65NI c  1972Li10,1971Li23: E=2.9 MeV deuteron beam was produced from a Van de  
 65NI2c  Graaff accelerator at the Leningrad State University, St.Petersburg,   
 65NI3c  Russia. Targets were 100-200 |mg/cm{+2} 77.8% enriched {+64}Ni.        
 65NI4c  Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with a many-angle magnetic    
 65NI5c  analyzer (FWHM|?15 keV). Measured |s(E{-p},|q), |q{-cm}|?30|'-160|'.   
 65NI6c  Deduced levels, spectroscopic factor ratios from DWBA analysis. Note   
 65NI7c  that 1972Li10 have adopted level energies in 1967Te02 and L-transfers  
 65NI8c  in 1963Fu04.                                                           
 65NI c  1977St07: E=2.8 MeV. FWHM|?30 keV. Measured |s(E(p),|q),               
 65NI2c  |q=50|'-160|'. Deduced levels, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis
 65NI c  1983ScZL (thesis): E=25.54 MeV at Rheinischen Freidrich-Wilhelms-Univ, 
 65NI2c  Bonn. FWHM|?45 keV. Measured |s(E(p),|q), |q=4.6|'-85.6|'. Deduced     
 65NI3c  levels, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis          
 65NI c  2013Sc06,2013ScZZ: E=10 MeV deuteron beam was produced from Yale tandem
 65NI2c  accelerator of WNSL facility. Target was 160 |mg/cm{+2} {+62}Ni (91.0% 
 65NI3c  enriched). Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with a split-pole  
 65NI4c  Enge spectrograph (FWHM|?50 keV). Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced       
 65NI5c  levels, J, |p, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis. Comparison    
 65NI6c  with shell-model calculations. Cross section are from 2013ScZZ         
 65NI c  (pol d,p) measurements:                                                
 65NI c  1973TyZZ (thesis): E=10 MeV at University of Winsconsin. Measured      
 65NI2c  |s(E(p),|q) and analyzing powers, |q|?20|'-130|'. Deduced levels, J,   
 65NI3c  |p from DWBA analysis                                                  
 65NI c  1991We07: E=2.7, 3.0, 3.3 MeV at Warsaw University. Reaction products  
 65NI2c  were detected with three surface-barrier detectors (FWHM|?22 keV).     
 65NI3c  Measured |s(|q). Deduced rms radii for single-particle neutron states  
 65NI4c  using the single-particle potential method.                            
 65NI c  Others: 1962Pa11, 1965Bo36, 1967Le01, 1968Gr18, 1968Gr23, 2009Le14     
 65NI c  For measurement of spectroscopic factors in continuum-bound states see 
 65NI2c  1983ScZL.                                                              
