 65CU    62NI(A,P)                     2001NY01,1972BU17         25NDS    202505
 65CU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65CU c  2001Ny01: E=25 MeV |a beam was produced from the Niels Bohr Institute  
 65CU2c  Tandem accelerator. Target was 99.8% enriched {+62}Ni with a thickness 
 65CU3c  of about 65 |mg/cm{+2}. Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with  
 65CU4c  the NBI multigap magnetic spectrometer (FHWM|?25 keV). Measured        
 65CU5c  |s(E{-p}, |q), |q{-cm}=7.5|' to 77.5|' in steps of 5|'. Deduced levels,
 65CU6c  J, |p, level spins and parities. The j-dependence of cross sections was
 65CU7c  used to achieve firmer spin assignments.                               
 65CU c  1972Bu17, 1975Se14: E=19.3-19.4 MeV |a beams were produced from the    
 65CU2c  U-120 cyclotron of the Institute for Atomic Physics, Bucharest. Target 
 65CU3c  was >98% enriched {+62}Ni with a thickness of about 1 mg/cm{+2}.       
 65CU4c  Reaction products were detected with a Si(Li) detector (FWHM=150-200   
 65CU5c  keV). Measured |s(E{-p},|q), |q{-cm}=10|'-130|'. Deduced levels, J, |p,
