 65CU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65CU c  1994Ri07 (also 1991Ri08): E=82.3-443 MeV electron beams were produced  
 65CU2c  from the medium-energy electron accelerator (MEA) at the NIKHEF-K      
 65CU3c  electron-scattering facility. Target was a metallic foil of {+65}Cu    
 65CU4c  enriched to 99.2%. Scattered electrons were momentum-analyzed with     
 65CU5c  a high-resolution Q2D spectrometer (FWHM=20-33 keV for forward angles, 
 65CU6c  and 40 keV for backward angles). Measured E(e). Deduced levels         
 65CU c  2010De09: E=120 MeV electron beam was produced from the LUE-300 linear 
 65CU2c  electron accelerator of Kharkiv Institute for Physics and Technology.  
 65CU3c  Target was 97.8% enriched {+65}Cu. Measured E(e), I(e), form factors.  
 65CU4c  Deduced levels, transition strengths. Comparisons with available data. 
 65CU5c  The authors also present re-analysis of data reported in 1988Ra11.     
 65CU c  Others: 1973KlZG, 1976PoZR, 1977Po18, 1985Ob02, 1987Sa44, 1988Ra11,    
 65CU2c  1988Ka31                                                               
