 65CU c  Note that most of relative intensity values (normalized to I|g=100 for 
 65CU2c  771|g) from 2000Ko51 are inconsistent with those in 1983Di04, probably 
 65CU3c  due to different level populations at different beam energies. To      
 65CU4c  preserve the intensity data in 2000Ko51 (less complete than 1983Di04), 
 65CU5c  the evaluator has put data from 2000Ko51 in a separate dataset:        
 65CU6c  {+65}Cu(n,n'|g) E=fast.                                                
 65CU c  1983Di04: E=0.7-6.0 MeV (mostly 4.85 MeV) neutron beams were produced  
 65CU2c  via {+2}H(d,n) reaction at the 5-MV Van de Graaff generator facility   
 65CU3c  and the Oak Ridge Electron Linear Accelerator (ORELA) facility. |g rays
 65CU4c  were detected with a Ge(Li) detector on both measurements. Measured    
 65CU5c  E|g, I|g, |g yields. Deduced levels, |g-ray branching ratios.          
 65CU6c  Comparisons with available data.                                       
 65CU c  1982De45, 1982El09: optical potential and deformation parameters from  
 65CU2c  {+65}Cu(n,n) and {+65}Cu(n,n')                                         
 65CU c  Others: 1982Sh28, 1971Fr05, 1970Fe04, 1968Da14                         
 65CU cG E,RI$From 1983Di04, unless otherwise noted. Intensities are relative   
 65CU2cG to I|g(770.7|g)=100. Values from 1983Di04 are measured at E(n)=4.85    
 65CU3cG MeV, |q=125|' and absolute values of cross sections are determined     
 65CU4cG by multiplying relative I|g values by 0.20 {I4} mb/sr (1983Di04).      
 65CU cG E(E)$Possible multiplet (1983Di04).                                    
 65CU cG E(X)$Transition unplaced in 1983Di04; tentatively placed by the        
 65CU2cG evaluator based on the placement of a similar |g in 2000Ko51           
 65CU cG RI(Y)$From the branching ratios shown in Fig.6 of 1983Di04 of the two  
 65CU2cG placements of each of 924.5|g, 1271.0|g and 2123.0|g, it seems that the
 65CU3cG authors have split the total I|g(924.5|g)=17.4 {I12}, I|g(1271.0|g)=6.0
 65CU4cG {I11} and I|g(2123.0|g)=6.1 {I11} in half                              
 65CU cG RI(Z)$From the branching ratios shown in Fig.6 of 1983Di04 of 1262.6|g 
 65CU2cG and 1163.7|g, it seems that the authors have split I|g(1262.6|g)=48.2  
 65CU3cG {I17} listed in Table 2 in half, assigned to each component of this |g 
 65CU4cG doublet.                                                               
