 65CU c  1967Br10: E=10.89 MeV proton beam was produced from the Harwell tandem 
 65CU2c  generator. Target was 99.4% enriched {+65}Cu with a thickness of 100   
 65CU3c  |mg/cm{+2} on a carbon backing. Scattered protons were                 
 65CU4c  momentum-analyzed with the ARRE Harwell single-channel magnetic        
 65CU5c  spectrography (FWHM=11 keV). Measured |s(E(p)). Deduced levels.        
 65CU6c  Comparisons with available data.                                       
 65CU c  1966Mc10: E=17.5 MeV proton beam was produced from the Princeton fm    
 65CU2c  cyclotron. Scattered protons were detected with surface-barrier        
 65CU3c  detectors (FWHM|?40 keV) Measured |s(E(p),|q), |q{-cm}|?25|'-100|'.    
 65CU4c  Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, deformation parameters from DWBA   
 65CU5c  analysis.                                                              
 65CU c  1957Ma23: E=6.51 MeV proton beam was produced from MIT electrostatic   
