 65CU c  1977Ha13: E=5.25 and 6.0 MeV proton beams were produced from the T11/25
 65CU2c  tandem Van de Graaff accelerator of the NRC Demokritos. Target was a   
 65CU3c  3.5 mg/cm{+2} self-supporting copper foil (enriched to 99.69% in       
 65CU4c  {+65}Cu). |g rays were detected with two Ge(Li) detectors. Measured    
 65CU5c  E|g, I|g, |g(|q), Doppler-shift attenuation. Deduced levels, J, |p,    
 65CU6c  T{-1/2}, |g-ray branching ratios, multipolarities and mixing ratios,   
 65CU7c  transition strengths. Comparisons with available data and theoretical  
 65CU8c  calculations.                                                          
 65CU c  1968Sm07: E=6.5 MeV proton beam was produced from the MIT-ONR Van de   
 65CU2c  Graaff accelerator. Target was 99.7% enriched {+65}Cu with a thickness 
 65CU3c  of about 250-280 |mg/cm{+2}. Scattered protons were momentum-analyzed  
 65CU4c  with the MIT multiple-gap magnetic spectrograph; |g rays were detected 
 65CU5c  with a NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E|g, I|g, p|g-coin. Deduced levels,  
 65CU6c  J, |p, |g-ray branching ratios.                                        
