 65CU c  2006Be34: measured E|g, I|g, with a planar HPGe detector and X         
 65CU2c  rays with a Si(Li) detector. Deduced absolute |g-ray emission          
 65CU3c  probability for 1116|g from an international EUROMET exercise          
 65CU4c  which includes results of nine participants. See also 2005BeZX         
 65CU c  2023Ha16: measured E|g, I|g, X-rays with a Silicon Drift Detector      
 65CU2c  centered inside the Modular Total Absorption Spectrometer (MTAS).      
 65CU3c  Deduced electron capture branches proceeding through excited states    
 65CU4c  versus those to the ground state.                                      
 65CU c  2014Bo01: measured precise E|g of 1115|g with a HPGe detector at       
 65CU2c  Diakoniekrankenhaus Schwabisch Hall                                    
 65CU c  1972De24: {+65}Zn source was prepared by electro-deposition onto a     
 65CU2c  10-20 |mg/cm{+2} thick VYNS foil. |g rays were detected with a NaI     
 65CU3c  detector; X rays, electrons and |b{++} particles were detected with a  
 65CU4c  4|p-proportional gas-flow counter. Measured E|g, I|g, I|b{++},         
 65CU5c  |b|g-coin, |g(t). Deduced parent T{-1/2}, absolute |g-ray and |b{++}   
 65CU6c  emission probabilities.                                                
 65CU c  2006Bo01: standardization of {+65}Zn |e decay using 4|p(LS)|b|g-coin   
 65CU2c  at LNHB. Deduced {+65}Zn T{-1/2}                                       
 65CU c  2006Ko31: measured T{-1/2}, absolute |g-ray emission probability       
 65CU2c  with 4|p|b|g-coin. 2006Ko31 is part of EUROMET exercise in 2006Be34    
 65CU3c  and the %I|g result in 2006Ko31 has been taken into account in         
 65CU4c  2006Be34                                                               
 65CU c  2005Iw01: measured absolute intensity of 1116|g using 4|p|b|g-coin.    
 65CU2c  Participant of EUROMET exercise in 2006Be34 and the result is          
 65CU3c  taken into account in 2006Be34                                         
 65CU c  2003Lu06: measured absolute intensity of 1116|g and {+65}Zn T{-1/2}    
 65CU2c  at LNHB. Participant of EUROMET exercise in 2006Be34                   
 65CU c  1996Gr13: standardization of {+65}Zn |e decay using 4|p|b|g-coin.      
 65CU c  1994Al53: measured |g-ray emission probability relative to I|g of      
 65CU2c  661.7|g from {+137}Cs decay using Cd-Te detectors in situ |g           
 65CU3c  spectrometer. I|g(1115.6|g)/I|g(661.7|g)=0.89 {I6}.                    
 65CU c  1994Ar22: measured E (K ray) and I(K X ray) with a Si(Li) detector     
 65CU2c  at BESSY electron storage ring.                                        
 65CU c  1994Le29: measured K|b/K|a ratio of X-ray emission probability         
 65CU c  1994So25, 1992Ba66: measured K-shell fluorescence yield                
 65CU c  1991Sy01: measured K-shell ionization probability of 2.2|*10{+-3} {I4} 
 65CU2c  using a triple coincidence spectrometer.                               
 65CU c  1990Ku11: measured K/|b{++} ratio using single and coincidence         
 65CU2c  counting with Ge(Li), Si(Li), NaI detectors.                           
 65CU c  1990Sc08: measured E|g, I|g, x-ray, 4|p|b|g coincidences               
 65CU2c  two Ge(Li) detectors for |g rays and a Si(Li) detector for |b          
 65CU3c  particles at PTB, Germany. Deduced absolute emission probability for   
 65CU4c  1116|g                                                                 
