 65CU    64NI(P,P),(P,P'),(P,N):RES    1970BR33,1969GU07         25NDS    202505
 65CU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65CU c  1970Br33: (p,p),(p,n) E|?3.1-3.3 MeV protons were produced from the    
 65CU2c  TUNL 3-MV Van de Graaff lab. Target was 97.9% enriched {+64}Ni on a    
 65CU3c  carbon backing. Charged particles were detected with surface-barrier   
 65CU4c  (FWHM=300-450 keV); neutrons were detected with two banks of BF{-3}    
 65CU5c  filled counters. Measured |s(E,|q), |q{-lab}=90|', 120|', 135|' and    
 65CU6c  160|'. Deduced IAR levels, J, |p, proton and neutron widths from       
 65CU7c  Breit-Wigner analysis and R-matrix analysis for 51 resonances          
 65CU8c  from E(p)(lab)=3.114 to 3283                                           
 65CU c  1969Gu07: (p,p),(p,p'),(p,n): E(p)=2.5-8.7 MeV. Measured |s(E,|q).     
 65CU2c  Deduced IAR levels, L(p), widths for 18 resonances from E(p)(lab)=3123 
 65CU3c  to 7086. 1969Gu07 is from the same laboratory as 1966Bo26              
 65CU c  1971Mo16: (p,p),(p,n) E=3.1-3.3 MeV protons were produced from the     
 65CU2c  TUNL 3-MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Target was 2 |mg/cm{+2} 98%       
 65CU3c  enriched {+64}Ni on a carbon backing. Detectors are the same as those  
 65CU4c  in 1970Br33. Measured |s(E,|q), |q{-lab}=90|', 120|', 135|', 160|'.    
 65CU5c  Deduced IAR levels, proton and neutron widths for 15 resonances        
 65CU6c  from E(p)(lab)=3198 to 3229. 1971Mo16 is a further study of the        
 65CU7c  analog fragments corresponding to 63, 1/2- level in {+65}Ni            
 65CU c  1966Bo26: (p,n) E(p)|<8 MeV from a Van de Graaff tandem. Target was    
 65CU2c  {+64}Ni with a thickness of about 0.2 mg/cm{+2} on a gold backing.     
 65CU3c  Neutrons were detected with a neutron counter (FWHM|?100 keV).         
 65CU4c  Measured |s(E(p)). Deduced IAR levels for 12 resonances from           
 65CU5c  E(p)(lab)=3104 to 7724                                                 
 65CU c  1972Ra23: (p,p),(p,p'): E(p)=3.1-5.3 MeV from the Universite Laval     
 65CU2c  |eN Van de Graaff generator. Target was 99% enriched self-supporting   
 65CU3c  {+64}Ni with a thickness of 50-250 |mg/cm{+2}. Scattered protons were  
 65CU4c  detected with four surface-barrier detectors (FWHM=25 keV). Measured   
 65CU5c  |s(E,E{-p},|q), |q{-lab}=90|', 140|', 150|' and 160|'. Deduced IAR     
 65CU6c  levels proton widths for 6 resonances up to E(p)(lab)=5.1 MeV.         
 65CU c  1966Ga14: (p,p),(p,p') E(p)|?3.2-3.6 MeV. Measured |s(E(p)). Deduced   
 65CU2c  widths for 2 resonances.                                               
 65CU c  1973TyZZ: (pol p,p): E(p)=3-7 MeV. Measured |s(E,|q) and analyzing     
 65CU2c  powers, |q{-lab}=120|' and 150|'. Deduced widths, J|p                  
 65CU c  1978Be40: (p,p),(p,p'),(p,p'|g): E(p)=5.0-6.2 MeV protons were         
 65CU2c  produced from the FN Tandem of the Institute for the Atomic Physics    
 65CU3c  in Bucharest. Target was isotopically enriched {+64}Ni with a thickness
 65CU4c  of about 200 |mg/cm{+2}. Scattered protons were detected with three    
 65CU5c  silicon surface-barrier detectors and |g rays were detected with a     
 65CU6c  NaI detector. Measured |s(E,|q) at |q{-lab}=90|', 110|', 125|', 141|', 
 65CU7c  and 160|', p|g(|q). Deduced IAR levels, J, |p, proton widths, L(p).    
 65CU c  1979Gu17: (p,n|g) E(p)=3.86-3.94 MeV. Measured |s(E(p)). Deduced       
 65CU2c  partial width for E(p)=3896 resonance.                                 
 65CU c  1976Le09: (p,n) E(p)|?2.67 MeV. Measured neutron time-of-flight for    
 65CU2c  a resonance which is 2.7 eV above the (p,n) threshold.                 
 65CU dL $Note that 1969Gu07 and 1966Bo26 report E(p)(c.m.) values which have   
 65CU2dL been converted to E(p)(lab) by the evaluator, as quoted in this dataset
 65CU cL $E(p)(lab), |G{-p}, and |G{-n} under comments are from 1970Br33 (values
 65CU2cL with uncertainties from 1971Mo16) up to 10686 level (E(p)(lab)=3283),  
 65CU3cL and from 1969Gu07 for levels above that, unless otherwise noted. |G(p')
 65CU4cL is for inelastically scattered proton to 1346, 2+ level in {+64}Ni.    
 65CU5cL Note that |G(p) and |G(n) values in 1971Mo16 are both obtained         
 65CU6cL independently from fits to the (p,p) and (p,n) data while in 1970Br33, 
 65CU7cL |G(p) is from fits but |G(n) from |G-|G(p) with |G values not listed   
