 65CU c  1974Cu02 (also 1974Le20): E=48 MeV {+12}C and E=56 MeV {+16}O beams    
 65CU2c  were produced from the Saclay FN tandem Van de Graaff. Target was 100  
 65CU3c  |mg/cm{+2} 99% enriched {+64}Ni on a 20 |mg/cm{+2} carbon backing.     
 65CU4c  Reaction products were detected with two |DE-E counter telescopes each 
 65CU5c  consisting of two surface-barrier silicon detectors (FWHM=250 keV for  
 65CU6c  {+15}N and 200 keV for {+11}B). Measured |s(E,|q), |q{-cm}=15|'-65|'.  
 65CU7c  Deduced levels, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis. 
 65CU c  See 1974Cu02 for full discussion of DWBA analyses and spectroscopic    
 65CU2c  values.                                                                
