 65ZN dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 28-Aug-2024)          
 65ZN d  Corrected by E. Browne (g.s. |g-ray sequence). 12-22-2009.             
 65ZN c  Adapted from the XUNDL dataset for 2001Mu24, compiled by R. Zywina and 
 65ZN2c  B. Singh (McMaster) on July 4, 2001.                                   
 65ZN c  2001Mu24,2001Mu33: E=65 MeV {+16}O beam was produced from the Nuclear  
 65ZN2c  Science Centre 15 UD pelletron. Target was 1 mg/cm{+2} natural Cr on a 
 65ZN3c  gold backing. |g rays were detected with the Gamma Detector Array (GDA)
 65ZN4c  consisting of 12 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors; charged particles  
 65ZN5c  were detected with the 4|p Charged Particle Detector Array (CPDA)      
 65ZN6c  consisting of 14 phoswich |DE-E detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,          
 65ZN7c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO). Deduced levels, J, |p, band structures.      
 65ZN8c  Comparisons with Total Routhian Surface calculations.                  
 65ZN cG $DCO values under comments are obtained by gating on a stretched       
 65ZN2cG transition. Expected DCO values are 1.0 for a stretched quadrupole     
 65ZN3cG transition, 0.4 to 0.6 for a stretched dipole transition, and 0.6 to   
 65ZN4cG 0.8 for a mixed transition. A dipole transition with |DJ=0             
 65ZN5cG (non-stretched) could also have DCO close to 1.0.                      
 65ZN cG E(E)$Poor fit; uncertainty multiplied by a factor in the fitting       
 65ZN cG E(F)$Very poor fit and omitted in the fitting                          
 65ZN cG E,RI$From 2001Mu24. Uncertainty in energy of 0.1 keV assigned for I|g>2
