 65ZN    66ZN(P,D)                     1976VaYX,1966MC15         25NDS    202505
 65ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65ZN c  Target J|p({+66}Zn g.s.)=0+                                            
 65ZN c  1976VaYX: E=35 MeV proton beam was produced from the MSU cyclotron.    
 65ZN2c  Target was isotopically enriched {+66}Zn. Reaction products were       
 65ZN3c  momentum-analyzed with an Enge split-pole spectrograph (FWHM=4-7 keV)  
 65ZN4c  for energy spectra and with a delay-line proportional counter          
 65ZN5c  system (FWHM=13-15) for |s(|q). Measured |s(E(d),|q), |q{-cm}=3|'-60|'.
 65ZN6c  Deduced levels                                                         
 65ZN c  1966Mc15: E=17.5 MeV proton beam was produced from the Princeton       
 65ZN2c  cyclotron. Target was about 1 mg/cm{+2} isotopically enriched {+64}Zn  
 65ZN3c  foil. Reaction products were detected with silicon surface barrier     
 65ZN4c  detectors (FWHM|?70 keV). Measured |s(E{-d},|q), |q{-cm}|?15|'-140|.   
 65ZN5c  Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA    
 65ZN6c  analysis.                                                              
 65ZN cL E$From 1976VaYX, unless otherwise noted. Uncertainty is not reported   
 65ZN2cL in 1976VaYX but could be estimated to around 5 keV from the resolution 
 65ZN3cL in the spectrum.                                                       
 65ZN cL L,S$From DWBA analysis of |s(|q) (1966Mc15). C{+2}S is obtained from   
 65ZN2cL d|s/d|W(exp)=N|*C{+2}S|*d|s/d|W(DWBA), where N is the normalization    
 65ZN3cL factor. Original values in 1966Mc15 are obtained by the authors using  
 65ZN4cL N=1.0, and the quoted values in this dataset are from the              
 65ZN5cL renormalization by the evaluator of those original values, using the   
 65ZN6cL recommended normalization factor N=2.29 for (p,d) in 1977En02. Average 
 65ZN6cL values for the two spin possibilities are given, except as noted.      
