 65ZN    66ZN(3HE,A)                   1971BE42                  25NDS    202505
 65ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65ZN c  Target J|p({+66}Zn g.s.)=0+                                            
 65ZN c  1971Be42: E({+3}He)=18 MeV from the Heidelberg E(n) Tandem accelerator.
 65ZN2c  Target was 98.55% isotopically enriched {+66}Zn. Reaction products     
 65ZN3c  were momentum-analyzed with a broad-range magnetic spectrograph        
 65ZN4c  (FWHM|?40 keV). Measured |s(E|a,|q), |q{-cm}=5|'-35|'. Deduced levels, 
 65ZN5c  L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis. Uncertainty in  
 65ZN6c  cross-section is about 15%                                             
 65ZN c  1967Bo39: E({+3}He)=33 MeV from Argonne 60-inch cyclotron. Target was  
 65ZN2c  97.8% enriched {+66}Zn. Reaction products were detected with a counter 
 65ZN3c  telescope of surface barrier detectors (FWHM|?100 keV). Measured       
 65ZN4c  |s(E|a,|q), |q{-cm}=15|'-40|'. Deduced levels, L-transfers,            
 65ZN5c  spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis                               
 65ZN cL $Spectroscopic factor is obtained using d|s/d|W(exp)=N|*C{+2}S|*\      
 65ZN2cL d|s/d|W(DWBA), where N is normalization factor. N=35 is used in        
 65ZN3cL 1971Be42, larger than the recommended N=23 in 1977En02                 
 65ZN cL E$From 1971Be42                                                        
 65ZN cL L,S$From DWBA analysis of |s(|q) data in 1971Be42. Quoted values of    
 65ZN2cL C{+2}S are for J|p=3/2- where L=1, 5/2+ (L=2), 7/2- (L=3) and (L=4),   
 65ZN3cL except as noted. These values must be considered as approximate in     
 65ZN4cL absolute terms since they have been calculated using a normalization   
 65ZN5cL factor of 35 (1971Be42) which is somewhat larger than the recommended  
 65ZN6cL value of 23 (1977En02). Comparison with {+66}Zn(p,d) data suggest      
 65ZN7cL C{+2}S should not be increased further.                                
