 65ZN    62NI(A,NG)                    1974NI01,1978NE02,1978KO1125NDS    202505
 65ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65ZN c  Also include data of {+56}Fe({+12}C,2pn|g) from 1975ChYJ and 1978Ne02  
 65ZN c  1974Ni01: E|a|?14 MeV from Reseach Institute for Physics, Stockholm.   
 65ZN2c  Target was 0.5-1.0 mg/cm{+2} isotopically enriched {+62}Ni.            
 65ZN3c  |g rays were detected with Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,        
 65ZN4c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q), |g(lin pol). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray        
 65ZN5c  multipolarities, mixing ratios.                                        
 65ZN c  1978Ne02: E|a=14-24 MeV from Notre Dame FN tandem. Target was 1.0      
 65ZN2c  mg/cm{+2} {+62}Ni. |g rays were detected with two Ge(Li) detectors.    
 65ZN3c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,           
 65ZN4c  |g-ray multipolarities, mixing ratios. Comparisons with available      
 65ZN5c  data. 1978Ne02 also measured |g|g-coin with {+56}Fe({+12}C,2pn|g),     
 65ZN6c  but no details are given.                                              
 65ZN c  1978Ko11: E|a=8.0-14.0 MeV from Oliver Lodge Laboratory. Same setup    
 65ZN2c  as 1977Lo03. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q), |g(lin pol),        
 65ZN3c  Doppler-shift attenuation. Deduced levels, J, |p, T{-1/2}, |g-ray      
 65ZN4c  branching ratios, multipolarities, mixing ratios.                      
 65ZN c  1977Lo03: E|a=6.5-17 MeV from Oliver Lodge Laboratory at University of 
 65ZN2c  Liverpool. Target was 98.7% enriched {+62}Ni. |g rays were detected    
 65ZN3c  with a three-Ge(Li) Compton polarimeter and an escape-suppressed       
 65ZN4c  spectrometer. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q), |g(lin pol),       
 65ZN5c  Doppler-shift attenuation. Deduced levels, J, |p, T{-1/2}, |g-ray      
 65ZN6c  branching ratios, multipolarities, mixing ratios.                      
 65ZN c  1975We08,1975We21: E|a=8.5 and 14 MeV from McMaster FN tandem. Target  
 65ZN2c  was isotopically enriched Ni metal. |g rays were detected with two     
 65ZN3c  Ge(Li) detectors. Measured |g(|q,H,t) and |g(|q). Deduced g-factors,   
 65ZN4c  |g-ray mixing ratios.                                                  
 65ZN c  1977Ch14: E|a=8.2 MeV from the Lyon University 4 MV Van de Graaff      
 65ZN2c  accelerator. Target was 99.5% enriched {+62}Ni. |g rays were detected  
 65ZN3c  with a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g, Doppler-shift attenuation.  
 65ZN4c  Deduced levels, T{-1/2}. 1977Ch14 also report data on {+65}Cu(p,n|g)   
 65ZN5c  A 20% uncertainty in stopping power theory is already included by      
 65ZN6c  the authors in T{-1/2} results.                                        
 65ZN c  1975ChYJ: {+56}Fe({+12}C,2pn|g) (probably); measured |g yields, |g|g   
 65ZN2c  coincidences and |g(|q); no details of results but level scheme is     
 65ZN3c  given                                                                  
