 65GA    9BE(70SE,65GAG)               2015NI01                  25NDS    202505
 65GA  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65GA c  Adapted from the XUNDL dataset for 2015Ni01, compiled by J. Chen       
 65GA2c  (NSCL, MSU) on January 26, 2015                                        
 65GA c  Includes {+9}Be({+69}As,65gag)                                         
 65GA d  Edited by B. Singh (McMaster), Jan 28, 2015                            
 65GA c  2015Ni01: E=175 MeV/nucleon {+78}Kr primary beam was produced from the 
 65GA2c  Coupled Cyclotron Facility at the National Superconducting Cyclotron   
 65GA3c  Laboratory (NSCL) and fragmented on a 399 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be production  
 65GA4c  target. The secondary beams of {+70}Se and {+69}As were selected using 
 65GA5c  the A1900 fragment separator and had typical intensities of 3.6|*10{+5}
 65GA6c  pps and 3.8|*10{+5} pps, respectively, and velocities of approximately 
 65GA7c  0.39 light-speed after target. The secondary target was 96 mg/cm{+2}   
 65GA8c  {+9}Be housed at the target position of the S800 spectrograph. Reaction
 65GA9c  products were identified on an event-by-event basis from energy-loss   
 65GAAc  and time-of-flight information using an ionization chamber and plastic 
 65GABc  scintillators, respectively. |g rays were measured by the SeGA array of
 65GACc  segmented high-purity germanium detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g-ray   
 65GADc  line shapes. Deduced levels, lifetimes using the |g-ray line-shape     
 65GAEc  method. Comparisons with shell model calculations.                     
 65GA cG E,RI$From 2015Ni01                                                     
 65GA cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g data, assuming 1 keV                   
 65GA2cL uncertainty for each |g ray                                            
 65GA cL J$From Adopted Levels                                                  
 65GA cL T$Lifetimes were extracted by comparing the experimental |g-ray        
 65GA2cL lineshapes spectra after Doppler-broadening correction to GEANT        
 65GA3cL simulations (2015Ni01). The effect of lifetimes on the                 
 65GA4cL Doppler-reconstructed lineshapes of |g-ray spectra at relativistic     
 65GA5cL recoil energies is to cause |g emissions at different locations along  
 65GA6cL the beam axis in the target, which results in different                
 65GA7cL Doppler-broadening corrections that distort the lineshapes.            
