 65GA dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 28-Aug-2024)          
 65GA c  1980Ka08: E=39 MeV {+12}C beam was produced from the E(n) tandem       
 65GA2c  accelerator at ORNL. Target was 0.72 mg/cm{+2} enriched {+58}Ni on a Pt
 65GA3c  backing. |g rays were detected with the two Ge(Li) detectors. Measured 
 65GA4c  E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q), |g|g(|q)(DCO), Doppler-shift attenuation. 
 65GA5c  Deduced levels, J, |p, T{-1/2}, |g-ray multipolarities, mixing ratios. 
 65GA6c  1980Ka08 also measured I|g, |g(|q) with {+60}Ni({+7}Li,2n|g) reaction  
 65GA7c  at E=18-21 MeV. See details in that dataset.                           
 65GA c  Other (HI,X|g) measurements which don't have much data:                
 65GA c  1980ZoZZ: {+54}Fe({+14}N,n2p|g) E=40 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,
 65GA2c  |g(|q), |g(lin pol). Deduced levels, J, |p, band structure.            
