 65GE    12C(58NI,ANG)                 1997SO06                  25NDS    202505
 65GE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen$CIT=NDS 202, 59 (2025)$CUT=25-Feb-2025$           
 65GE dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 17-Jul-2024)          
 65GE c  Adapted from the XUNDL dataset of 1997So06, compiled by G. Reed and    
 65GE2c  B. Singh (McMaster) on July 9, 2001.                                   
 65GE c  1997So06: E=261 MeV {+58}Ni beam was produced from the tandem          
 65GE2c  accelerator of Niels Bohr Institute, Denmark. Target was 1.5 mg/cm{+2} 
 65GE3c  {+12}C. |g rays were detected with the NORDBALL array comprised of 15  
 65GE4c  BGO-shielded Ge detectors, a 30-element gamma-ray calorimeter of       
 65GE5c  BaF{-2} crystals; neutrons were detected with 11 neutron detectors;    
 65GE6c  charged particles were detected with a 4|p array consisting of 21 |dE  
 65GE7c  type Si detectors. Measured E|g, |g|g-coin, particle-n-|g|g-coin, and  
 65GE8c  |g(|q) intensity ratios. Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray multipolarities.
 65GE9c  Comparisons with interacting boson-fermion model calculations. Details 
 65GEac  about the data are not available in 1997So06, except for a level scheme
 65GE cG E$From Fig.1 of 1997So06. No tabulated data are given in 1997So06.     
 65GE cG M$Assignments are not explicitly given in 1997So06 but could have been 
 65GE2cG made by authors with their spin assignments based on measured |g(|q),  
 65GE3cG implied by a general statement about parity assignments in 1997So06:   
 65GE4cG definite parities were assigned to the excited states, if one of their 
 65GE5cG deexciting transitions were stretched E2 or mixed M1/E2 transitions,   
 65GE6cG while in the case of pure dipole transitions only tentative parities   
 65GE7cG were ascribed. The assignments quoted here are made by the evaluator   
 65GE8cG based on that statement, but with the magnetic/electric characters     
 65GE9cG being removed because of no supporting data for those characters in    
 65GEacG 1997So06, and are all placed in parentheses by the evaluator and       
 65GEbcG should be considered as tentative due to lack of the details of the    
 65GEccG |g(|q) data.                                                           
 65GE cG E(A)$Strong |g-ray, as seen in Fig.1 of 1997So06                       
 65GE cG E(B)$Medium intensity |g-ray, as seen in Fig.1 of 1997So06             
 65GE cG E(X)$Placed differently in Adopted Gammas                              
 65GE cL $Level scheme here is from Fig.1 of 1997So06, and is partially         
